### W3: forcing-test hang guard (create; Task; priority Low; labels `rec-2026-11-16`, `test`; marker `REC-LND-16NOV-W3`)
SUMMARY-W3: Optional hardening of the new forwarded-proof forcing test: guard its first request with the same 30 second wait, so a future test server that waits for the whole pipeline fails in 30 seconds instead of hanging

BEGIN BODY-W3
BLUF: The forcing test added by pull request 325 holds a test filter open after the pipeline and then sends a request. If a later test server made the request wait for the whole pipeline, the request would wait for the held filter forever, and the test's try and finally could not release it. Today this does not happen (measured). This is the independent review's optional follow-up.
Recommendation: Wrap the first request of the forcing test (`ForwardedProofTests.cs:178`) in the same 30 second wait the watch read already uses (`ForwardedProofTests.cs:277`), so a hang becomes a failure.
Detail: Measured by the independent review: with the write removed the target test goes red in 31 seconds through the existing guard, so only the first request lacks one. Not blocking; do when the test server or the test host is next upgraded, or decline.
Done when: the guard is added, or the item is recorded as declined.
Records: entry C-<<CE3>> in the project's clarifications record.
Marker: [REC-LND-16NOV-W3]
END BODY-W3

